					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1722371&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605861462" alt="Shaggydredlocks" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1722371)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/shaggydredlocks" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1722371); return false;" >Shaggydredlocks</a></span> <span class="odate time_1493951582 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">05 May 2017 02:33</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2811287">
									

<p>I really, really want to upvote for a well-written villain. Craggs is utterly reprehensible, but quite affable at the same time; she's definitely the star of this show.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">My issue lies with E-1261's backstory explanation: It's far too showy, to the point of being overwrought. I feel so overwhelmed with the bite-sized stream of torture that I just end up feeling numb, and wanting to scroll. I think it seems a little forced, and already covers things one could glean from exposition given by the other characters or the scenario in general.</span></p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I suggest moving through her incarceration/experimentation in a less literal/direct fashion. More haze, confusion, lost periods of time. Sensations. Only being able to recount things on a fringe-level. <em>Imply</em> the conditions, rather than list them off. Then, the scene where she kills, of course, can be as vivid as-is currently written (as she remembers these events distinctly). This kind of tone-down would move this away from (imo) trying <em>too</em> hard to be 'horrible'. (Also, the 'I watched myself&#8230;I did those things' bit is a little over-the-top for my tastes as well.)</span></p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">This would have secured a downvote, but I'll be damned if Craggs doesn't more than make up for it. Neutral.</span></p>
<p>ETA: Whelp, that solved my problems! Good job on quite possibly the only CI character I've ever liked (not that I've read a ton of them, but still). +1</p>

