			<div class="content" id="post-content-2836472">
									

<p>So, here's the way I wrote it. Multiple interpretations are possible.</p>
<p>E-1260 and E-1261 are sleeper agents for the Chaos Insurgency. However, E-1261 is a reluctant, and unaware member of this operation, as prisoner-test subject-'Mike'. To complicate things, 1261 blames the Chaos Insurgency and especially Craggs for making her this way.</p>
<p>The initial breakout of Foundation custody is with 1260 controlling/proxying through 1261 - up until the point that 1261 collapses the first time. Craggs has known about this the entire time, and planned ahead - all the controllers can ALSO be controlled, directly, by Craggs, through the same technology. Craggs forces 1260 to strangle himself, assuming that 1261 is basically catatonic without a controller.</p>
<p>Instead, 1261 wakes up, realizes the opportunity she has, and lunges at Craggs on her own initiative - which Craggs, always being one step ahead, thwarts anyway.</p>
<p>In short, &quot;No one leaves the Chaos Insurgency.&quot; are words from 1260, proxying through 1261. If you check the transcripts, E-1261 never swears, ever, until the last document. Check the dates. If this is present day, she went through all of this when she was barely a teenager. It's supposed to be a radical change of tone to indicate that this actually isn't 1261.</p>

							</div>

								
					
